# 🧪 8. Real-World Autopilot Scenarios

## 📝 Scenario 1 — Device Not Assigned to Profile

### **Cause**
Device imported but not assigned to a group.

### **Fix**
- Add device to Autopilot group  
- Assign profile  
- Sync device  

### **Ticket Note**
Autopilot failed due to missing group assignment. Added device to correct group and synced. Profile applied successfully.

---

## 📝 Scenario 2 — Autopilot Stuck on “Setting up your device”

### **Cause**
Network blocking Autopilot endpoints.

### **Fix**
- Switch to open network  
- Restart provisioning  
- Confirm profile assignment  

### **Ticket Note**
Autopilot stuck due to restricted network. Switched to open network and provisioning completed successfully.

---

## 📝 Scenario 3 — Apps Not Installing During Provisioning

### **Cause**
Incorrect Win32 detection rule.

### **Fix**
- Update detection rule  
- Reassign app  
- Re-run provisioning  

### **Ticket Note**
Win32 app failed during Autopilot due to incorrect detection rule. Updated rule and re-provisioned device. App installed successfully.

---

## 📝 Scenario 4 — White Glove Pre-Provisioning Failure

### **Cause**
TPM not ready.

### **Fix**
- Reboot device  
- Check TPM status  
- Retry pre-provisioning  

### **Ticket Note**
White Glove failed due to TPM not initialised. Restarted device and TPM became ready. Pre-provisioning completed successfully.

